 ## From playtests
 
-| Idea | Rank | Raised | Notes |
-| --- | --- | --- | --- |
-| Limited horse boost to catch up with a train | Scheduled (Phase 2 M3, on by default) | Devlin, M3 playtest, 2026-10-09 | A short burst above top speed with a cooldown or a stamina cost. It fits the reserved `handlingModel` variant group (stamina, speed tiers). |
-| Resistance while boarding: guards on the train shoot at the rider, perhaps only at higher heat | High | Devlin, M3 playtest, 2026-10-09 | Needs combat (phase 3) and heat (phase 2). A heat threshold in config would let heat make the approach harder as well as the run. |
-| More track layouts and terrain, to see whether runs vary enough to stay fun | High (extra maps in [PR #10](https://github.com/devlinjunker/train-robber/pull/10)) | Devlin, M3 playtest, 2026-10-09 | The map pipeline already supports several routes per map, speed zones and terrain zones. This needs new maps drawn in Tiled. See also "World and schedule" below. |
-| Moving between cars | Scheduled (Phase 2 M2) | Devlin, M3 playtest, 2026-10-09 | Multi-car interiors were deferred to phase 2. |
-| Moving onto the roof | High (built: sneaking PR 3, [PR #36](https://github.com/devlinjunker/train-robber/pull/36)) | Devlin, M3 playtest, 2026-10-09 | The requirements make the roof a traversal route for bypassing or surrounding a car. After the Phase 2 M3 guards playtest (2026-10-17) it is being designed with side ledges and end platforms in the [Outside the train](https://claude.ai/code/artifact/5a6a4ecc-15cc-4747-9326-52c30881cc98) doc, to sneak past guards. |
-| A deliberate camera and zoom design for the final game (how far out while riding, aboard and boarding); free wheel zoom is fine for the alpha | Medium | Devlin, M3 playtest, 2026-10-09 | Pairs with the renderer choice under "Presentation, input and platform". The boarding meter was enlarged for the alpha at the same time. |
-| Track playtest responses in the repo (answers to each PR's playtest questions, and Playtests page exports, kept as files) | Medium | Devlin, 2026-10-10 | For now the answers go in a PR comment and run history stays local on the Playtests page, with an optional GitHub issue. Doing this means picking a folder layout and possibly a GitHub Action that collects `playtest` issues. |
-| Online multiplayer, to look at once all the initial trains work and have been playtested, because it gives the game more staying power | Medium | Devlin, 2026-10-10 | Gang play is already listed under "Presentation, input and platform" below; this sets when to think about it. |
-| A rival gangs mode | Low | Devlin's wife, via Devlin, 2026-10-10 | How it works is undecided: other gangs racing you for the same train, or players on opposing gangs. Depends on multiplayer, or on AI gangs if it is single-player. |
-| A real horse that rides the terrain to reach the train after a whistle, and with it the world-structure test (separate map vs continuous world) | Required (alpha test variant) | Devlin, Phase 2 plan review, 2026-10-11 | Phase 2 uses a scripted horse. |
-| Landing on foot when a guard throws you off the train, then whistling for the horse | Medium | Devlin, Phase 2 plan review, 2026-10-11 | |
-| Heat levels: past thresholds guards spot you faster, and at full heat every car is on alert | High | Devlin, Phase 2 plan review, 2026-10-11 | Phase 2 heat only speeds up the clock. |
-| Riding back to pick up loot spilled on a good mount | Low | Devlin, Phase 2 plan review, 2026-10-11 | |
-| A way for wanted level to come down, such as a clean getaway lowering it by one, or decay over runs or time | Required (before progression) | Devlin, Phase 2 plan review, 2026-10-11 | Phase 2 has no way down. |
-| Side ladders as entry points beside doors, so you can board straight onto the roof (or a side ledge) from the horse | High | Devlin, Phase 2 plan review, 2026-10-11; confirmed for later 2026-10-17 | Not part of the first roof and ledge work: you board through doors and climb out from inside (Devlin, Outside the train doc, question O6). Mail car layouts mark roof access so ladders can be added without redoing them. |
-| Low bridges and signal arms over the line, as a hazard for anyone up on the roofs | Medium | Devlin, sneaking PR 3 request, 2026-10-21 | Noted as a later idea while building roofs; trackside rocks can't reach the roof today. |
-| Terrain height that changes riding: slopes slow the horse uphill and speed it downhill, ledges you can jump off, and track grades that change train speed | Medium | Devlin, mud and boulders playtest, 2026-10-12 | Touches the sim's physics, every map test, the golden replay and decided design-doc values, so it needs planning like a milestone. The visual-only height layer (cliffs and hills you can see, sim unchanged) is being built first, and its height data is what this would build on. |
-| Zoom mostly out of the player's control (a small nudge at most), and zooming out when riding on top of a hill because you can see farther | Medium | Devlin, 2026-10-14 | A direction for the "deliberate camera and zoom design" row above. Hill height comes from the visual height layer in [PR #25](https://github.com/devlinjunker/train-robber/pull/25); today the run allows a ±0.3 nudge around a fixed run zoom (`?runZoomRange=`). |
-| No train arrows in the final game: ride the plains looking for tracks and a train to board, unless you have a timetable upgrade | Medium | Devlin, 2026-10-14 | The arrows and minimap stay for the alpha. Ties into "Timetables showing upcoming trains, bought with loot" below and the outfitter and hideout map room in the [progression exploration doc](https://claude.ai/code/artifact/3f07eb5c-ed70-4843-aff0-b629edc4f361). Probably wants a config switch so it can be playtested against the arrows. |
-| Train whistles as directional sound cues you hear while riding, which sometimes briefly show the train's arrow | Medium | Devlin, 2026-10-14 | The way to find trains without permanent arrows. Needs positional audio, so it pairs with "Sound and music" below. |
-| Health that belongs to the whole time on a map, not to the run: you start the map with full health, and crashing into things before you find and commit to a train already hurts you | Medium | Devlin, 2026-10-14 | Today health matters only once a run starts. Changes how crash and scrape damage ([PR #12](https://github.com/devlinjunker/train-robber/pull/12)) and train hit damage ([PR #26](https://github.com/devlinjunker/train-robber/pull/26)) apply, and fits the "No train arrows" row, where riding around looking for a train becomes part of the risk. |
-| A better inventory: the current one (I, then 1-9 drops) is a strip of text boxes along the bottom that works but doesn't feel good | Medium | Devlin, Phase 2 M2 playtest, 2026-10-14 | Built in [PR #17](https://github.com/devlinjunker/train-robber/pull/17) as a stopgap. Open questions: item icons, showing weight and value at a glance, dropping by click or drag, and whether it should pause or stay live during a run. |
-| Random wildlife on the map: predators (bears, mountain lions) that attack you while you ride, and herds (cattle, buffalo, horses) that get in your way and sometimes block the track enough to slow the train down | Medium | Devlin, 2026-10-20 | Attacks need a horse or rider that can be hurt (see "A horse that can be hurt" and "Health that belongs to the whole time on a map"). A herd that slows the train would change train speed, which today comes only from track speed zones, so it touches the sim and the golden replay. Pairs with the cattle train's stampedes under "Trains" and could be scattered by the map generator. |
-| Dust kicked up from the gap between the horse and the train, and wheel rumble that gets louder as you close in, so you can feel how close you are | Low | Devlin, PR #20 playtest, 2026-10-12 | Atmosphere on top of the far-side cues in PR #20 (stretched see-through hole and the glow on the car edge). |
