+What's coming next for Train Robber: the rest of Phase 2, Phase 3, the generated-maps work (the G series) and multiplayer. Last updated 2026-10-27.
+
+The repo has the full detail: the [requirements](https://github.com/devlinjunker/train-robber/blob/main/docs/requirements.md) (the phase roadmap), the [technical design](https://github.com/devlinjunker/train-robber/blob/main/docs/technical-design.md) and the [phase plans](https://github.com/devlinjunker/train-robber/tree/main/docs/plans). Ideas that aren't scheduled yet are on the [Ideas](Ideas) page.
+
+## Where things stand
+
+| Track | Done | In progress | Next |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Phase 1: riding and boarding | Everything; the gate passed | | |
+| Phase 2: the mail train | M1 countdown and heat, M2 mail train and loot, M3 guards and boost, M4 extraction, sneaking PRs 1 and 2 | Sneaking PR 3: roofs ([#36](https://github.com/devlinjunker/train-robber/pull/36), waiting on a playtest) | M5 wanted level and saving, M6 tests and the Phase 2 playtest |
+| Phase 3: military payroll | | | A plan first; no plan exists yet |
+| Multiplayer | Groundwork in the sim since Phase 0 | | A network test right after Phase 3; full multiplayer at the end |
+| Generated maps | G0 docs, G1 generator ([#31](https://github.com/devlinjunker/train-robber/pull/31)), G2 checks over seeds (inside G1), G3 the open line ([#34](https://github.com/devlinjunker/train-robber/pull/34)) | G4 chunks ([#38](https://github.com/devlinjunker/train-robber/pull/38), waiting on a playtest), then G5 streaming | G6 towns and timetables |
+
+Versions follow `0.<phase>.<milestone>`: Phase 2 M5 will be 0.2.5, and Phase 3 starts at 0.3.x.
+
+## Phase 2: what's left
+
+Phase 2 is the first full run on the mail train. Its gate is to compare short and medium runs and pick a target run length.
+
+**Sneaking PR 3: train roofs** ([#36](https://github.com/devlinjunker/train-robber/pull/36), draft)
+- Ladders at both ends of two of every three cars, and walking, running and crouching on the roofs.
+- Guards in the car below hear you on the roof; guards can see you at the roof edge and climb up after you.
+- Jumping the gap between cars, and slipping on curves.
+- Side ladders (boarding straight onto the roof from the horse) are left for Phase 3.
+
+**M5: wanted level, saving and score**
+- Your progress is saved in the browser between runs: wanted level, bank and lifetime earnings. A broken or newer save is backed up and reset, with a notice.
+- Wanted level (0 to 5) goes up with your robberies and puts more guards on the trains.
+- Every way a run ends (extracted, expired, died, cancelled) has clear rules for what you keep.
+- A local leaderboard: score, seed, settings and date. `?wanted=` plays any wanted level for practice, and those runs save nothing.
+- An end-of-run summary screen: outcome, loot banked, time, heat, the change in wanted level, and quick retry.
+
+**M6: tests, tuning and the playtest**
+- A recorded golden run on the mail train, and a test that saves and restores a run in the middle of an extraction.
+- Bots over 1,000 seeds: an idle bot that must run out of time, and a looter that must sometimes get away.
+- Run reports: run length, how often runs finish, time to first loot and heat at the end.
+- Ready-made presets for the main questions, linked from [Playtesting](Playtesting).
+- **The Phase 2 gate:** compare short and medium runs and pick a target run length.
+
+## Phase 3: the military payroll train and combat
+
+Phase 3 adds fighting. Its gate: combat feels good, and the two health models have been compared. There's no Phase 3 plan yet; like Phases 1 and 2, it starts with a plan and a review of its open questions.
+
+- **The military payroll train.** Soldiers as guards and a big payout. It's the train that favours fighting, but sneaking should still work.
+- **Full guard AI.** This builds on the Phase 2 guards: they notice you by sight and sound, go from suspicious to alert, and call others, which raises the alarm.
+- **Combat.** Aim and fire with the mouse, with bullets that travel and can miss, and a close-range melee attack. Car layouts already mark what blocks sight and shots and how much cover each spot gives.
+- **Health.** A real health bar replaces the placeholder. A "downed" variant is tried against it: you get about 6 s to recover, and you lose your loot only if that runs out.
+- **Moved here from Phase 2.** Guards shooting at you while you board at high heat, and side ladders onto the roof.
+- **Heat and guards.** On the open line the clock no longer speeds up with heat, so heat should change how guards behave instead (from the G3 playtest).
+
+**Open questions for the Phase 3 plan:** ammo limits (the alpha default is unlimited), knocking guards out as well as killing them, healing items as loot, and how to keep sneaking workable on a train built for fighting.
+
+## Generated maps: the G series
+
+The plan is the [procedural maps options doc](https://claude.ai/artifact/7qncafySjNAx8pW92fVcXg), "a day on the line". Its 16 review decisions are recorded in its "Decisions from review" table and in the requirements under "World structure: a day on the line".
+
+**A day on the line.** The game has three time scales:
+- **A train:** one robbery, a few minutes.
+- **A day:** a run, about 12 minutes from dawn to dusk, with several trains passing.
+- **A career:** many days, until your outlaw dies (permadeath is a variant).
+
+The world is one seeded railway that runs on forever, with terrain around it, towns every few thousand tiles and trains on a seeded timetable. You find the track, scout or wait, and pick a train, sometimes the wrong or a tougher one. You tell train types apart by sight at first, and later by rumours, timetables and a spyglass. At dusk you pick a camp off the line, and tomorrow starts from there. Each career gets a new world.
+
+**Daily and friends.** The free demo is a daily day: everyone gets the same seed, with a streak, a wanted poster and a community line that everyone moves along together. Your record carries into the full game when you buy it. Owners can ride the daily as a gang with friends who don't own the game, and the occasional free gang weekend lets free players ride together. Ghost riders were declined.
+
+The plan has five stages, and each one ends with a playtest gate:
+
